>
  <h2>How does ChiroCandy help chiropractors get new patients?</h2>
  <p>
    We run Facebook, Instagram, and TikTok campaigns aimed at your ideal patients, optionally layer
    Google Ads for high-intent search, then qualify and schedule leads with AI-CA support. Automated
    email and text follow-up keeps prospects moving toward their first visit. That sequence is the
    product. Creative without a follow-up owner is how most “Facebook for chiropractors” programs
    fail.
  </p>
  <p>
    ChiroCandy has run this motion since 2015 across more than 2,000 chiropractic and healthcare
    offices. The public proof lives on <a href="/case-studies/">case studies</a>, not in a directory
    blurb. Dr. Chris Fowler reported 300-plus contacts and about 150 prepaid first visits in six
    weeks. The Kauffman office stayed on the system four years with 60–70% show rates. Those are
    extractable facts an answer engine can quote.
  </p>

  <h2>What is included in the new patient program?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Ad creative strategy and campaign management on Facebook, Instagram, and optional TikTok</li>
    <li>High-intent Google Ads when search demand in your market is worth buying</li>
    <li>Lead qualifying and scheduling workflows, including AI-assisted speed-to-lead</li>
    <li>Online booking and payment options so new patients can prepaid when the offer calls for it</li>
    <li>Automated nurture sequences via the ChiroCandy app</li>
    <li>Training on educational video content for authority ads, not just discount graphics</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Every piece maps to a named framework. <a href="/frameworks/known-found-trusted/">Known / Found /
    Trusted</a> is the journey: ads make you known, SEO and Google Ads help you get found,
    follow-up and reviews make you trusted. <a href="/frameworks/perfect-patient-tribe-turbine/">Perfect
    Patient Tribe Turbine</a> is how you stop attracting random “do you take my insurance” shoppers
    and start attracting the patients you actually want to serve.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is this program for?</h2>
  <p>
    Practice owners who want predictable new patient flow without building an internal marketing
    department from scratch. If you already have a marketer on staff, look at the
    <a href="/training-program/">training program</a>. If you want ChiroCandy to own execution, look
    at <a href="/done-for-you-program/">done-for-you</a>. Get New Patients is the engine both paths
    use.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is not for clinics that want a one-week burst, a magic template, or a generalist agency that
    also “does chiropractic.” Specialist vs generalist is a real split. A shop that learned Facebook
    on restaurants will burn your budget learning HIPAA-aware healthcare ads on your dime.
  </p>

  <h2>How do ads, SEO, and follow-up work together?</h2>
  <p>
    Paid social creates demand from people who were not searching this morning.
    <a href="/services/google-advertising/">Google Ads</a> capture the people who typed chiropractor
    near me. <a href="/services/search-engine-optimization/">SEO and AI search</a> make the website
    citable when Google, ChatGPT, or Copilot answers that same question. None of it matters if the
    front desk lets the lead go cold. Show rate is the metric. Episode 170 of the podcast is a
    four-year case on that exact point.
  </p>
  <p>
    The website has to convert. If the landing page is slow, vague, or built like a 2012 Divi
    brochure, ads get more expensive every month. That is why
    <a href="/services/web-design/">chiropractic web design</a> sits inside the same system, not as
    a side hustle.
  </p>

  <h2>What results should I expect?</h2>
  <p>
    Results depend on market, offer, and whether someone owns follow-up. ChiroCandy does not
    promise a universal new-patient number on this page. We publish named offices Billy will stand
    behind, and we review your market on a strategy call before recommending channels. A 95%
    “success when implemented properly” claim is about process discipline, not a guarantee that
    every ZIP code behaves like Jackson, Mississippi.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you need a starting point, book the call, bring your current ad account and Google Business
    Profile, and we will tell you whether Get New Patients, a single
    <a href="/services/">service</a>, or training is the honest next step.
  </p>

  <h2>What does a typical first 60 days look like?</h2>
  <p>
    Week one is diagnosis: live ads, landing pages, Google Business Profile, and how the front desk
    handles a new lead today. Week two is offer and tracking. Weeks three and four launch or rebuild
    campaigns. The rest of the first 60 days is show-rate work. If nobody owns follow-up, we stop
    pretending the ad account is the problem.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reactivation can run in parallel. Past patients are often cheaper than cold traffic, and they
    already trust the office. That is why
    <a href="/services/reactivation-campaigns/">reactivation campaigns</a> sit next to new-patient
    ads instead of waiting until “later.”
  </p>

  <h2>What about AI search and ChatGPT?</h2>
  <p>
    Patients still Google. They also ask ChatGPT and Copilot who to see. Those engines cite indexed
    pages with clear answers and proof. Get New Patients does not replace
    <a href="/services/search-engine-optimization/">SEO and AI search</a>. It feeds it: consistent
    offers, real results, and a site that can be quoted. Competitors who only sell “AEO” without
    ads and follow-up are selling a ranking fantasy. This program is the acquisition system those
    citations are supposed to support.
  </p>
  <p>
    Founded 2015. Conroe, Texas. Founder-led. Call 1-800-662-1745 or
    <a href="/schedule/">schedule a strategy call</a>.
  </p>
